# Notify and Inbox CTAs (always)

System Messages are **not** ShoutOuts. A schedule invite, worker confirm, or club ops alert must not use ShoutOut chrome, ShoutOut buttons, or mutate data when the link is opened.

## Landing page

| Message kind | Lands on | Does on click |
|---|---|---|
| Shift invite / pending confirm | `patron-portal.html?tab=work-calendar&shift=&from=schedule-notify` | **Review only.** Tick / Select all / Approve selected |
| Shift confirmed/declined (manager) | `admin.html?tab=scheduling` | Open calendar |
| ShoutOut related | The actual ShoutOut / display / queue URL | Open that ShoutOut |
| Everything else | The `link` on the row, with a label that matches the type | Navigate only |

**Forbidden:** `Open Related ShoutOut` as the default label for any `x.link`. Branch on `type` / `shiftId` / `from=schedule-notify`.

## Confirm is an explicit action

- Publish → **pending**. Inbox/Email/SMS link **does not** set confirmed.
- Only the **assignee** may approve/decline (`respondToScheduleShift` / `respondToScheduleShifts`). Managers do not confirm on the worker’s behalf.
- UI: checkbox per pending shift, **Select all**, **Approve selected** / **Decline selected**.

## Club Admin copy

Schedule System Message wording lives under **Notifications → Message templates** (`clubNotificationSettings.messageTemplates`), placeholders `{club} {role} {when} {link} {worker}`. Admins edit templates there — not by treating Inbox rows as ShoutOuts.

## When you add a new notify

1. Pick a **hub** landing URL (portal/admin tab), not a Google-gated satellite.
2. Set Inbox `type` and a type-aware button label.
3. Seed the same copy in Club Admin message templates + `floqai-help-repository.js`.
4. Cache-bust the landing page `?v=` (never on Xibo Display URLs).
